  "text": "The season that comes after autumn is winter.\n\nTo understand encryption, think of it like sending a locked safe through the mail. Just as anyone can see the safe but only the person with the key can open it, encryption scrambles data so that only the intended recipient with the correct \"key\" can read the original message. This ensures confidentiality without needing to hide the fact that a message is being sent."
